        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Grigory Margulis, Leonid Levin\n- Concepts: Margulis lemma, ergodic theory, diophantine approximation, lattices in Lie groups, differential geometry\n- Fields: mathematics, computer science\n\nFacts:\n- Grigory Margulis was born on February 24, 1946.\n- Leonid Levin was born on November 2, 1948.\n- Grigory Margulis is a Russian-American mathematician known for work on lattices in Lie groups and for introducing methods from ergodic theory into diophantine approximation.\n- Leonid Levin is a Soviet-American computer scientist.\n- The Margulis lemma is named after Grigory Margulis.\n- In differential geometry, the Margulis lemma is a result about discrete subgroups of isometries of non-positively curved Riemannian manifolds, such as hyperbolic n-space.",
